Fix: HIT_DIVERGED boundary-rescue could call truncate_computed_blocks with a
retry boundary deeper than a lagging group's actual locally cached hit,
crashing the engine (`AssertionError: assert num_blocks <= len(group_blocks)`
in v1/core/kv_cache_manager.py's truncate_computed_blocks).

Found in production: server ran a real deployment (both restore-corruption
fixes applied -- kv-offload-restore-mamba-conv-spec-reserve.patch,
kv-offload-store-optimistic-completed-tokens.patch) for ~30 minutes of
multiple simultaneous conversations, then hit this assertion and crashed
the EngineCore. This patch is a fix to the pre-existing
hit-diverged-boundary-rescue.patch's rescue mechanism, found and fixed
in the same investigation (RESTORE_CORRUPTION_PLAN*.md /
RESULTS-restore-corruption-*.md) but is NOT one of that investigation's
two corruption bugs and is unrelated to either of their root causes --
it is a distinct, pre-existing logic bug in the rescue path itself,
newly exposed by longer/heavier real-world multi-conversation load
than this deployment had previously sustained.

Root cause: `get_computed_blocks_for_connector` (v1/core/kv_cache_manager.py)
populates `new_computed_blocks` from `find_longest_cache_hit_per_group`,
which fills each KV-cache-group's block list to THAT group's own local hit
depth -- not padded to the deepest group's depth. For a hybrid Mamba+
attention model, a lagging group's list (typically Mamba's single running
checkpoint) can therefore be genuinely shorter than the full-attention
group's. When full-attention's hit is deeper than a lagging group's
(`hit_diverged`) and the connector finds no external tokens at the
attention-based boundary, the existing rescue in v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
(`schedule()`) re-queries the connector ONE align-size chunk (832 tokens)
below the attention boundary and, on success, truncates ALL groups'
locally cached blocks to that retry boundary via `truncate_computed_blocks`.
That rescue distance -- exactly one align-size chunk -- assumes the
lagging group is never more than one chunk behind full attention. Under
sustained eviction pressure (long-running, multiple concurrent
conversations competing for GPU-resident blocks) a lagging group's hit
can fall more than one chunk behind, so the one-chunk-down retry boundary
still exceeds that group's own cached block-list length, and
truncate_computed_blocks's `assert num_blocks <= len(group_blocks)` fires
for that group, crashing the engine.

Fix: before computing the retry boundary, compute the shortest group's
own locally cached depth directly from `new_computed_blocks.blocks`
(`min(len(group_blocks) for group_blocks in new_computed_blocks.blocks)
* self.block_size`, floored to the nearest align-size chunk) and cap the
one-chunk-down retry boundary at that value. This is a pure narrowing: it
never asks the connector or `truncate_computed_blocks` for a boundary
deeper than what a diverged group can actually support. If the true
shallowest group is more than one chunk behind, `retry_local` now comes
out <= 0 and the existing "not rescued" fallback (full reconcile via
`get_computed_blocks()`, discarding down to the boundary every group
agrees on, with its existing WARNING log) takes over -- exactly the same
safe fallback already used when the connector's retry lookup itself
fails. No HIT_DIVERGED safety semantics are weakened: a rescue is now
attempted only when it can structurally succeed, and the fallback path
that already exists for "the tier genuinely can't back the boundary" is
reused unchanged for "the local blocks genuinely can't back the
boundary" too.

Verification: syntax-checked (`ast.parse`), `verify.sh --no-server`
green (all patches apply). NOT yet re-verified under sustained
multi-conversation production load (the exact condition that exposed
the bug) -- next restart should watch for another
`HIT_DIVERGED RESCUED`/`HIT_DIVERGED RECONCILE` log line (both now
expected instead of a crash) if the same divergence recurs.
--- a/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
+++ b/v1/core/sched/scheduler.py
@@ -844,10 +844,34 @@
                                 # aligned to every group's block size.
                                 and align_size % self.block_size == 0
                             ):
-                                retry_local = (
+                                # Stepping down by exactly one align-size chunk
+                                # from the deepest (attention) boundary is only
+                                # safe when every diverged group's own local
+                                # hit is no more than one chunk shallower.
+                                # Under sustained eviction pressure a lagging
+                                # group (e.g. Mamba's single-checkpoint state)
+                                # can lag by MORE than one chunk -- its entry
+                                # in `new_computed_blocks` (populated per-group
+                                # by find_longest_cache_hit_per_group) is then
+                                # shorter than one chunk down from
+                                # block_aligned_local, and truncate_computed_
+                                # blocks below would assert. Cap the retry
+                                # boundary at the shortest group's own locally
+                                # cached depth so it never asks for more than
+                                # that group actually has.
+                                min_group_tokens = (
+                                    min(
+                                        len(group_blocks)
+                                        for group_blocks in new_computed_blocks.blocks
+                                    )
+                                    * self.block_size
+                                )
+                                retry_local = min(
                                     block_aligned_local
                                     - block_aligned_local % align_size
-                                    - align_size
+                                    - align_size,
+                                    min_group_tokens
+                                    - min_group_tokens % align_size,
                                 )
                                 if retry_local > 0:
                                     # Safe to repeat: get_num_new_matched_tokens
